1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,200
Okay the next unspoken rule is all about how to be in sync with the locals.
好，下一条不成文规则是怎样跟上当地人的节奏。

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:10,879
It's critical to understand if you want to be going to restaurants when they're actually open you don't want to be going to shops when they're all closed.
了解这一点很关键：你想去餐厅时它得开着，也不想去逛店时发现商店全关了。

3
00:00:10,879 --> 00:00:17,240
It's about how the spaniards kind of schedule their lives and how you should think about scheduling your day as a tourist.
这关乎西班牙人怎样安排生活，也关乎作为游客，你该怎样安排自己的一天。

4
00:00:17,240 --> 00:00:21,830
Okay so first up shops in the morning morning are often going to open later than maybe you're used to.
先说商店。讲者说，早上的开门时间可能比你习惯的晚。

5
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:25,480
They possibly won't open till about 10 10 30 or even 11 00 a m.
可能要到十点、十点半，甚至上午十一点才开。

6
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:31,120
But look if you want to get breakfast somewhere early you want to search on google or look around for a cafeteria.
不过如果想早点吃早餐，可以搜索或四处找一家 cafeteria。

7
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:38,230
A cafeteria will look like a tapas sp on the outside but it's actually somewhere that's going to open earlier often around 8 9 00 a m.
它外观看起来可能像小吃吧，但通常会早一点开，讲者说常在早上八九点左右。

8
00:00:38,240 --> 00:00:42,120
So you can grab breakfast cup of coffee and start your day that way.
这样你就能吃点早餐、喝杯咖啡，开启一天。

9
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:50,110
Oh and by the way this place this c t is closed today's monday so lots of restaurants also close on mondays be aware of that.
顺便说，这家字幕写作 c t 的店今天关门，因为是星期一。讲者说很多餐厅周一也会关门，要留意。

10
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:57,599
And then once the shops are open about 10 00 a m and the big cities and in the center they're going to stay open all day till maybe about 8 00 p m or so.
店铺上午十点左右开门后，大城市和市中心的店可能一直开到晚上八点左右。

11
00:00:57,599 --> 00:01:06,520
But in the neighborhoods like this neighborhood in madrid or in the small towns shops are going to open about 10 00 then they're going to close again at 2 for about 3 hours for a long lunch break.
但在像马德里这个社区这样的街区，或小城镇，商店可能十点开，下午两点又关门，午休约三小时。

12
00:01:06,520 --> 00:01:08,999
And then they'll open again at 5 00 until about 88.
然后下午五点重新开门，开到字幕写作 88 的时间，具体数字待确认。

13
00:01:08,999 --> 00:01:14,680
So right down the street it's it's now 3 00 all these shops are closed because they're having that 3 hour lunch break.
现在是三点，这条街上的店都关着，因为正在进行那段三小时的午休。

14
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:19,599
So that's one of the reasons why it makes sense to have lunch when the locals are having lunch at 2 p m p m.
这也是为什么在下午两点跟当地人一起吃午饭会比较合适。

15
00:01:19,599 --> 00:01:26,960
Because then you'll have a big long lunch maybe after that have a walk or a siesta and then by 5 00 p m you're up and about again and everything's open.
这样可以慢慢吃个午饭，再散步或午睡，到了下午五点又出来活动，店也都开了。

16
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:34,080
And if you're an early eater really the earliest that the kitchens will open here is 1 00 p m and they'll usually serve food until about 4 00 p m.
如果你吃饭较早，讲者说这里厨房最早下午一点开，一般供餐到下午四点。

17
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:41,840
And then when it comes to dinner tapas bars and restaurants usually aren't going to open them till about 8 8 30 and they'll serve food right through till till midnight.
晚餐方面，小吃吧和餐厅通常八点或八点半才开，然后一直供餐到午夜。

18
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:48,680
But beware you might see on google that some tapas bars say they're open all day from say midday till till midnight.
不过要留神：地图上有些小吃吧可能写从中午到午夜全天营业。

19
00:01:48,680 --> 00:01:52,680
But it's doesn't necessarily mean that the kitchen is open the entire time.
但这并不一定意味着厨房全程开着、一直供餐。

20
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:55,800
The kitchen might only be open from 12 00 to 4 00 and 8 onwards.
厨房可能只在十二点到四点、以及八点以后开。

21
00:01:55,800 --> 00:02:01,920
So you want to call them up and say what time does the kitchen open then you can make sure.
所以可以打电话问，厨房几点开始供餐，这样就能确认。

22
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:07,999
And finally there are all day kitchens where tapa spas will be serving food all day generally those are a little more touristy.
最后，也有全天供餐的厨房，小吃吧整天都卖吃的，讲者觉得这类地方通常更面向游客。

23
00:02:07,999 --> 00:02:14,360
But look if you're traveling with kids or whatever it makes sense right feel free to use them you have my permission.
不过如果带孩子旅行之类的，这样吃也很合理，尽管去吧，我准许了。

24
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:21,439
Okay next up let's tackle some unspoken transport rules that'll help you get around the cities that you're visiting.
接下来谈几条没明说的交通规则，帮助你在所到城市出行。

25
00:02:21,439 --> 00:02:28,200
First up when you're on the escalator make sure you stand on the right so that people who want to walk up and down can do so on the left.
首先，讲者说搭扶梯时站右侧，让想走上走下的人能从左侧通过。

26
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:34,350
That's really important and if you see an elevator only use it if you need it I e you have mobility issues.
这一点很重要。如果看到电梯，讲者建议在确有需要时才用，比如行动不便。

27
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:39,960
Or you're with a child or you have suitcases they're reserved for people who really need them.
或者带孩子、带行李箱，因为这些设施留给真正需要的人使用。

28
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:45,240
And remember when you're getting on the train make sure you stand back and let people to get out first.
记住，上火车时先往后站，让车里的人先出来。

29
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:57,640
Otherwise someone might give you a little shove or at least they might say uh sorry I almost broke my own roll.
否则可能有人轻推你一下，或至少会说点什么……抱歉，我差点违反自己刚说的规则。

30
00:02:57,640 --> 00:03:02,919
And if you're thinking of not using public transport and you're going to jump in a taxi or an uber maybe think twice.
如果你想不用公共交通，直接坐出租车或网约车，也许可以再想一想。

31
00:03:02,919 --> 00:03:08,200
I've seen people walk out of a of a tapa sp and jump right into a cab to get back to their hotel.
我见过有人走出小吃吧就直接钻进出租车，回他们的酒店。

32
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:13,720
And it takes them longer in the cab to get there than if they were just going to walk or take public transport.
而他们坐车过去花的时间，反而比步行或乘公共交通还长。

33
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:18,600
Because of the the the compactness and the traffic in these historic centers all over spain.
讲者认为，这是因为西班牙各地这些历史城区布局紧凑，而且有交通拥堵。
